---
import Slide from '@decks/templates/Slide.astro';

// The strongest slide in the deck, and the one to leave running while
// talking. The scorecard is computed from the settings rather than
// written down, so a panel can ask "what about keyboard only" and the
// answer is a toggle away instead of a claim.
//
// It opens on `drag`, which reads 1 of 4. The move is to walk to
// keyboard (3 of 4, and where most people stop) before landing on menu.
//
// nospec=1 drops the specimen so the audit can carry the slide: the
// panel alone is 620 x 543.
//
// align="top" is required, not cosmetic. Under the default centring the
// header is positioned absolutely so the body can centre on the real
// slide midpoint, and a panel this tall then renders straight over the
// subtitle. Top-aligned, the header stays in flow and the frame gets
// what is left: 1080 less 80 of padding, the header, and its 112px gap,
// which lands near 710. Hence scale 1.2, giving 800 x 708.
---

<Slide subtitle="Four inputs, one question" align="top">
	<div class="grid grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] items-start gap-12">
		<iframe
			src="/decks/2026-checklist-component/prototypes/c4-accessibility-bench?embed=1&scale=1.2&show=audit&nospec=1&reorder=drag&focus=object"
			title="Can you reorder a row: four inputs scored live"
			class="live-embed m-0! block h-[708px] w-[800px] max-h-none! max-w-none! border-0"
		></iframe>
		<div class="grid gap-13">
			<div class="text-strong text-5xl">
				The keyboard path was necessary and it was never sufficient.
			</div>
			<div>
				<div class="text-subdued text-xs font-medium uppercase">SC 2.5.7 asks for</div>
				<div class="text-strong mt-3 text-4xl font-medium">A single pointer</div>
				<div class="text-subdued mt-2 text-2xl">A keyboard is not one.</div>
			</div>
			<div class="text-subdued text-3xl">
				<span class="text-strong">The menu is the only path that covers all four.</span>
				It is also the smallest thing to build.
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</Slide>
